        "status": 503,
        "detail": "Managed geoprocessing on this host would be queued for a background loop that stops when the invocation ends. The request is refused instead of being accepted and never run. Native processes run on the GDAL worker. Managed processes run on a long-lived API host, or they finish inside the request without being queued.",
        "code": "dependency-unavailable",
        "capability": "jobs.runner",
        "missingDependency": "long-lived-host",
        "remediation": "Run managed geoprocessing on a long-lived host (local Docker or ECS). On this serverless cell, submit a native process so it runs on the GDAL worker. An operation that completes inside the request, without admission to the local job queue, is not refused by this check.",
        "remediationRef": "https://honua.io/docs/guides/deploy/cloud-deployments/#background-file-imports-run-on-aws-batch"
      }
    },
    "$comment": "The same request recorded while Redis was wired into the demo (2026-10-24, rolled back the same day). With Redis present the serverless cell still refuses managed processes: nothing stays up to drain the job queue (missingDependency long-lived-host)."
